  "scope": "An explicit C2 finite-Fourier XYZ prefix from shared endpoint jets.\n\nThe exact map is defined by the saved binary64 nodal two-jets and exact\nquintic Hermite interpolation, not by rounded power coefficients. The mean\nheight's nodal values are exact sums of saved per-span increments, avoiding\nloss from subtracting independently rounded cumulative heights. Other data\nare finite binary rationals. Numerical evaluation uses long double.\n\nThis is a representation and sampled-audit layer. It neither proves an\ninfinite tail nor converts sampled bounds into continuous certificates.\n",
  "mathematical_definition": "Exact shared nodal two-jet quintic Hermite, finite cylindrical Fourier modes 3j. All nodal constants and span increments are exact saved binary64 rationals. Mean height value at node i is the exact sum of increments before i; its saved cumulative array is for display only. Planar inlet and vertical first jet are imposed; second jet retains the adaptive chart transport, and a cylinder interface is not certified. Additionally all inlet height second jets are exactly zero. Thus direct upper/lower reflection is exactly C2 without a central cylinder; its inlet immersion follows from a nonzero planar angular tangent and the exact vertical first s jet.",
